[82415] [2026-01-15 21:26:13] [INFO] [ENGINE]  <--------- ENGINE SEND: COMATE_AGENT_UPDATE_MESSAGE {"data":{"type":"partial-message-data","conversationInfo":{"id":"586273fd-c7dd-4c60-9e4c-dbec9fa29bab","status":"Completed","type":"E2EBotConversation","utime":1768483573667,"ctime":1768483541469},"messages":[{"id":"04508caa-c240-4135-9551-005492a585f6","userMessageId":"15067425","reportedId":"5c14e622-b527-4c1a-8490-0ee2701c185f","agentInfo":{"avatar":"zulu","name":"Zulu"},"role":"assistant","status":"completed","content":{},"elements":[{"id":15067425,"type":"REASON","text":"**Designing the Database System**\n\nI'm currently grappling with the database selection aspect. Considering the user's needs, I'm leaning toward a modular design. This should allow seamless integration of various database types (MySQL, PostgreSQL, etc.) and versions. I'm focusing on defining clear interfaces for each database to handle version-specific differences in syntax.\n\n\n**Mapping User Requirements**\n\nI've been breaking down the requirements into actionable steps. My focus is on translating the user's needs into a practical system. The functionalities requested are clear: database selection, version handling, table definition input, and SQL generation. I've begun to define the interfaces and data structures needed to support these operations, prioritizing flexibility and extensibility.\n\n\n**Planning the Implementation**\n\nI've decided to prioritize a Python-based solution, leveraging Streamlit for a user-friendly web interface. I am sketching out the initial project structure, including directories for generators (SQL), data models, and the main application file. The core logic will focus on defining data models, SQL generation across various dialects, and handling data type mapping.\n\n\n**Structuring the Application**\n\nI'm now focusing on establishing the project's foundation. Initially, I'll use Python and Streamlit for the application. The goal is to quickly build a functional prototype. I'm setting up directories for code, generators, and data models. Then, I'll write the core classes for SQL generation, focusing on MySQL and PostgreSQL for the initial tests. Finally, I'll develop the Streamlit interface for user interaction and present clear instructions on how to start the app.\n\n\n","status":"success","discard":false,"startTime":1768483552133,"lastModifiedTime":1768483560647,"parentMessageId":""},{"id":"3beb72aa-5446-4e5c-af4d-a508fdcb44eb","type":"TEXT","status":"success","content":"这是一个非常实用的需求。为了快速构建这个交互式系统，我建议使用 **Python** 配合 **Streamlit** 库。Streamlit 非常适合快速搭建数据驱动的交互式 Web 应用，用户可以在网页上选择选项、输入表格信息，并实时看到生成的 SQL。\n\n我将按照以下计划为你构建这个系统：\n\n1.  **设计核心逻辑**：定义通用的表结构模型，并实现支持多数据库（如 MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite）的 SQL 生成器。\n2.  **构建交互界面**：使用 Streamlit 创建 Web 界面，包含数据库选择、表信息输入（动态添加字段）和 SQL 展示区域。\n3.  **实现功能**：\n    *   支持选择数据库类型（MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite）。\n    *   支持简单的版本区分（主要影响某些特定语法，初步实现通用语法）。\n    *   输入表名、列名、类型、长度、约束（主键、非空、自增）。\n    *   生成并展示 `CREATE TABLE` 语句。\n\n首先，我查看一下当前项目目录结构。\n\n","composer":{"markdown":"","tasks":[]},"discard":false,"isErrorMessage":false,"parentMessageId":""},{"id":"6968ead6e5bb2854a5a1f1a7","type":"TOOL_CALL","status":"success","toolName":"list_files","discard":false,"composer":{"markdown":"","tasks":[]},"workflowStatus":"success","displayParams":{"path":"~/ComateProjects/comate-zulu-demo-1768483535778"},"displayResult":{"fileCount":0},"parentMessageId":""},{"id":15067499,"type":"REASON","text":"**Planning the Project's Setup**\n\nI'm starting a new project, and the initial directory is empty. I plan to build a Streamlit application for SQL generation. The main file will be `sql_generator.py`, housing both the UI and the SQL generation logic. I'm focusing on Streamlit for the UI framework and custom logic for the SQL generation.\n\n\n","status":"success","discard":false,"startTime":1768483570244,"lastModifiedTime":1768483570244,"parentMessageId":""}]}]}}
